Z||000000||CanadianGT||06-04-2001||11:50 AM||||So I go on Sunday to go look at my car that the rebuilders here in Toronto has had now for over 2 month's, for what was supposed to be a 2 week job max.  He called me, as he said it was finaly done, and I could come see it running.  So I boot down there, only to hear him turning the car over, but it will not start.  He said that the previous day  he was having a problem with the manifolds starting to glow  bright red after 20 minutes of running the car.  I ASKED HIM to check the EGR(doubt it is that however as I bought A new tube and valve last year), cat, and vacum lines and computer codes, but he looked at me as some unknowledgable 18 year old.  He said that his computer code checker was at the shop next door which was closed and he could not check it until the next day when it opened.  I told him about shorting the system to get the codes to pop up on the dash, but he said that would not be a proper thing to do when you are running a business.  It seems to me that niether is having someones car for 2 months longer then they are supposed to have it.  Then I started to ask him about why the car was not starting now though, and he did not know.  Just as I was about to check for things like spark and fuel, he was checking the fuel pressure and realized It had none.  Moral of the story, is if you want the job  done right, you should take it to people who know Fiero's .  I will now only do work myself or take it to the Fiero shop here in Toronto from now on.  On top of that they have scratched my paint and gave my battery to someone else.  They were trying to tell me my battery was not holding a charge, but it in fact was not even my battery, as I have the bill for my battery still, and it is not the brand they are trying to give back to me. Good thing my dad is a lawyer........cause if I dont get some type of restitution, it looks like court will be the only way to go.  I'll let you know the name of the place when (IF I ever) get my car back.<BR>PeAcE<BR>Kyle<P>[This message has been edited by CanadianGT (edited 06-04-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by CanadianGT (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
